-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",120,{
[3809]="70065EAA\n1\tSpeak with Goldberry at her spring in the Old Forest\tFaranil carefully packed the young sapling into a pot and gave it to you with instructions to take the sapling into the Old Forest to speak with the River-maiden Goldberry.\n2\tSpeak with Tom Bombadil at his home in the Old Forest\tGoldberry directed your to meet with her again at Tom Bombadil's house deep within the Old Forest.\n3\tNurture your sapling at Old Man Willow\tTom hinted that you need bring the sapling to visit Old Man Willow, as something there will help the sapling grow into what it is meant to be.\n4\tTalk to Faranil\tHaving done all you were told it is now time to return the sapling to Faranil in the Ettenmoors as Tom suggested.\n",
[3810]="70065E98\n1\tTravel to Evendim and seek out Quickbough\tFaranil believes that it is time to speak with the Ent, Quickbough, about the sapling you have found. Though she knows the risk is that she will give the Ent false hope with this discovery.\n2\tTalk to Faranil\tYou spoke with Quickbough and it seems the Ent is given a new hope with your sapling. Return to the Ettenmoors and Faranil to tell them what occurred.\n",
[3811]="70065E9F\n1\tAsk Ned Claybrick at Hoarhallow if his plants are inquisitive\tMake your way to Hoarhallow and ask Ned Claybrick if he ever thinks that plants he tends seem inquisitive.\n2\tTalk to your sapling\tNed suggested that he speaks to his plants but he has never listened to them. Maybe there is something to what he said. Return to Glân Vraig and give it a try.\n3\tListen to your sapling\tYou talked to the sapling, but nothing seemed to change. Perhaps you should try listening.\n4\tSpeak with Faranil at Glân Vraig\tThough you heard nothing when listening to the sapling, it did seem that something stirred in the little plant. Let Faranil know.\n",
[3812]="70065EA4\n1\tMake your way to Hoarhallow and speak with Marigold Winterdown\tJourney to Hoarhallow and ask Marigold Winterdown if she knows of a way to brighten a flower or plant even further.\n2\tDance with your sapling\tMarigold told you to dance with plants and they will dance with you. Return to Glân Vraig and dance with your sapling.\n",
[3813]="70065E97\n1\tDefeat Cragstone Spiders ([see journal]/14)\tFaranil wants to eliminate the threat of the spiders that roam the Ettenmoors. The Cragstone brood is found far to the west. Make your way to them and cull the brood.\n2\tReturn to Glân Vraig and speak with Faranil\tReturn to Faranil at Glân Vraig and tell her that you have done what she asked, and that a great number of the Cragstone brood died this day.\n",
[3814]="70065E99\n1\tDefeat Darktide wolves ([see journal]/14)\tFaranil wants to help secure the future of the forests in the Ettenmoors by culling the Darktide wolves from the woods.\n2\tTalk to Faranil\tWith your effort to thin the numbers in the Darktide pack complete, you should return to Faranil and let her know of your efforts.\n",
[3815]="70065EB4\n1\tDeliver filtered earth to Faranil at Glân Vraig (total: 7)\tMake your way to the Hoardale River, specifically around Tol Ascarnen, and collect filtered soil from within the bellies of the nerbyg that make the banks their home.\n",
[3816]="70065EA5\n1\tCollect a phial of Hoarwell water at the first location\030Collect a phial of Hoarwell water at the second location\030Collect a phial of Hoarwell water at the third location\030Collect a phial of Hoarwell water at the fourth location\030Collect a phial of Hoarwell water at the fifth location\tFaranil marked your map with many locations within the Ettenmoors where you can collect some of the purest water that the Hoarwell provides. She then gave you phials, asking that they be filled at locations she marked for you.\n2\tDeliver the water to Faranil at Glân Vraig\tYou collected the phials of pure water from the Hoardale. Return them to Faranil at Glân Vraig.\n",
[3817]="70065EB6\n1\tDefeat the forces of Angmar (total: 15)\tFaranil suggested you make your way into the Ettenmoors and defeat the enemy that would pervert nature and destroy other saplings that may be growing in the wild.\n2\tReturn to Glân Vraig and speak with Faranil\tHaving completed your efforts against the enemies of nature, you should return to Faranil and tell her of your victory.\n",
[3818]="7006B560\n1\tDefeat Bok, the goblin leader at Grothum\tHead north and west of Glân Vraig. On the east side of the Ettendeep in Arador's end find and defeat the goblin leader Bok, in the village of Grothum and then return to Faranil.\n2\tTalk to Faranil\tBok is defeated. Return to Faranil at her post in Glân Vraig and inform her of your success.\n",
[3819]="70065EA7\n1\tSpeak with Faranil after completing Cultivation quests ([see journal]/20)\tFaranil asked that you return to her each day to see what new effort might strengthen your sapling. She is located in Glân Vraig, the foothold of the Free People in the Ettenmoors.\n",
[3820]="70032BE2\n1\tFind what is cultivating the mushrooms\tThe cultivator of the mushrooms is likely to be near the centre of the recently corrupted area. The corruption has spread quickly from the Foundations of Stone, and it is being helped and guided by something.\n2\tDefeat The Twisted One\tThe cultivator of the mushrooms is a terror from deep within the Foundations of Stone. The corruption has spread quickly from the Foundations of Stone, and it is being helped and guided by one of the nameless. This agent of corruption must have been sent here by something far more sinister....\n3\tReturn to Knakk\tKnakk is camped on the elevated walkway in the north-east corner of Redhorn Lodes. He will be eager to know his assessment was right, and that the cultivator of the mushrooms has been found and defeated.\n",
[3821]="70028447\n1\tDefeat Goblins in Nan Curunír (total: 8)\tGoblins can be found near the cave in western Nan Curunír. Ondor has asked you to thin the number of Goblins around the caves before venturing within.\n2\tTalk to Ondor in Nan Curunír\tOndor is near the caves in western Nan Curunír. You should return to Ondor with news of your success.\n",
[3822]="7004DA38\n1\tCollect Celeblam (total: 10)\tCeleblam flowers can be found in Eryn Lasgalen. Thranduil has asked you to gather Celeblam for the Elves of Eryn Lasgalen so that Thorlind can craft more of his healing draught.\n2\tTalk to Thranduil\tThranduil can be found in Felegoth. You should talk to Thranduil.\n",
[3823]="700272F9\n1\tTâl Methedras Oxen can be found on the far side of the lake, across from Tûr Morva.\t\n2\tBring the tough ox-skin to Rhus\tRhus is on the eastern shore of the lake in Tâl Methedras, by his tanning tools in Tûr Morva.\n3\tClean strips of leather in sudsy buckets (total: 3)\tBuckets of sudsy water are set out near Rhus in Tûr Morva. Rhus has asked you to help clean the leather strips he is soaking in the sudsy buckets.\n4\tTalk to Rhus in Tûr Morva\tRhus is by his tanning tools in Tûr Morva. You have cleaned several of the strips of leather that Rhus has been soaking and should now speak with the tanner about what he needs next.\n5\tBeat the stretched hides to improve their suitability for armour-making (total: 4)\tThere are hides stretched between poles near Rhus in Tûr Morva. Rhus wants you to beat the stretched hides in order to smooth them out for use in armour-making.\n6\tTalk to Rhus in Tûr Morva\tRhus is by his tools in Tûr Morva. You have helped Rhus considerably, and he wishes to speak with you.\n7\tBring treated ox-skins to Taf on the shore of the lake\tTaf is at the leather-working pavillion, north of Rhus's home and on the shore of the lake in Tâl Methedras. Rhus has given you treated ox-skins to bring to Taf.\n",
[3824]="700300A2\n1\tAsk Gandalf about the horse that stands near him\tGandalf is atop Treebeard's Hill, alongside a horse you have never seen before. Gandalf has one more thing to say to you.\n2\tReturn to Ashlimb to tell him of the hobbits' fate you may use the horse near Gandalf for swifter travel\tAshlimb is at the eastern edge of Fangorn's eaves, waiting to hear of the hobbits' fate. You should return to Ashlimb and convey Gandalf's tale of their meeting with Treebeard.\n3\tSearch the surrounding woods for another sleeping Ent\tEnts can be found throughout Fangorn. You should search north-east of Ashlimb for other Ents you can help, as Gandalf bid.\n",
[3825]="7005F6C0\n1\tFree ukhrâsh from traps at Lochan Dúv (total: 8)\tUkhrash-traps can be found at Lochan Dúv in Gloomingtarn. Hersegg has asked you to free ukhrâsh from traps at Lochan Dúv in the hope that releasing them will hinder the plans of the Iron Crown in Gloomingtarn.\n2\tTalk to Hersegg\tHersegg can be found in Gloomingtarn. You have freed many ukhrâsh from traps at Lochan Dúv and sent the Iron Crown into disarray. You should talk to Hersegg. NOTE: If you become separated from Hersegg, use her horn to call her to your side.\n",
[3826]="70039A11\n1\tSearch the fields east of Middlemead for Déorwald's apprentice\tDéorwald's apprentice can be found on the fields of Kingstead to the east of Middlemead and Folcbur's homestead. Déorwald believes his apprentice to be journeying to Pendlac's Farm on an unknown errand. You should find and speak to his apprentice.\n2\tConfront the Uruk War-leader\tThe Uruk War-leader can be found on the fields to the east of Middlemead. You have discovered the remains of Déorwald's apprentice, his horses, and his presumed murderer. You should confront and defeat the Uruk-hai responsible.\n3\tTalk to Déorwald\tDéorwald can be found at the traders' pavillion in central Middlemead. You have found Déorwald's apprentice slain by a vicious Uruk who spoke of mysterious things. You should return to Déorwald with this ill news.\n",
[3827]="70018FC0\n1\tCollect Orc filth from the banks of the Nimrodel (total: 5)\tThe soiled banks of the Nimrodel can be found north and south from Echad Andestel, along the banks of the stream. Dindirith has asked you to clean up the banks of the Nimrodel, sullied by the passage of the Orcs.\n2\tBring Orc filth to Dindirith\tDindirith is in Echad Andestel, west of the banks of Nimrodel and the border of Lórien. You have collected Orc filth from the banks of Nimrodel and should return now to Dindirith, as he asked.\n",
[3828]="70061F73\n1\tReturn stolen artifacts (quantity: see journal)\tArnail has asked you to return stolen items to graves within Haudh Nirui. Haudh Nirui is in the South Downs, in north-eastern Cardolan.\n2\tReturn to Arnail\tYou should let Arnail know that you have returned the stolen artifacts to the graves. Arnail is on the road near the Scurloc Farm, in the South Downs.\n",
[3829]="7001E9BE\n1\tDestroy ore carts (total: 3)\tGarmadh-maudhûl can be found to the north-east of Mithechad by following a trail that traverses up the mountain. Eirien has asked you to destroy the ore-carts which the Orcs at Garmadh-maudhûl are using to resupply Dol Guldur.\n2\tTalk to Eirien in Mithechad\tEirien is at Mithechad, south-west of Garmadh-maudhûl. You should return to Eirien and let her know that the ore-carts have been destroyed.\n",
[3830]="7002FDA6\n1\tCollect cuts of fish (total: 24)\tFish can be caught in the lake and river just east of Snowbourn. Héalac asked you to go fishing and bring him several dozen cuts of fish.\n2\tBring the cuts of fish to Héalac\tHéalac is at Snowbourn. Héalac will be pleased to get all of the cuts of fish you were able to catch.\n",
[3831]="70030E61\n1\tShoo Dudweld away from the food-stores with a stern ahem\030Shoo Ganburh away from the food-stores with a stern ahem\030Shoo Elfswith away from the food-stores with a stern ahem\tThe food-cart is near the kitchen of Snowbourn. As food is scarce, Fastred wants you to make sure that people wait and do not swarm the food-stores. Perhaps a stern ahem will do.\n2\tCollect prepared rations for the people of Snowbourn (total: 3)\tPrepared rations can be found inside the kitchen of Snowbourn. You should collect rations for the people of Snowbourn.\n3\tTalk to Dudweld\030Talk to Ganburh\030Talk to Elfswith\tDudweld, Ganburh, and Elfswith can be found throughout Snowbourn. You should distribute the food to Dudweld, Ganburh, and Elfswith.\n4\tTalk to Gísling\tGísling can be found in central Snowbourn. You should speak with Gísling and let him know you distributed the food as Fastred ordered.\n",
[3832]="70007F46\n1\tFind Vífill\tVífill is somewhere in the firewood grove down the road west of Noglond. Grímkell has asked you to go out and search for Vífill.\n2\tTalk to Grímkell Stonebearer\tGrímkell is at Noglond, east of the firewood grove. Vífill tells you to inform Grímkell of the presence of goblins in the firewood grove.\n",
[3833]="70039C11\n1\tDefeat the attacking Orcs\tOrcs are swarming the lumber-yard, east of Aldburg. Defeating the Orcs will ensure an easier foray to retake the lumber-yard.\n2\tDefeat the attacking Orcs (total: 10)\tOrcs are swarming the lumber-yard, east of Aldburg. Defeating the Orcs will ensure an easier foray to retake the lumber-yard.\n3\tCompleted\tMany Orcs were defeated by you while you were saving the lumber-yard.\n",
[3834]="70000CBC\n1\tDefeat Reykur\tReykur will likely be found at the furthest chambers of the ruins where the wights are encamped. Eriac has asked you to kill the gaunt-man Reykur, Ivar's captain among the wights. Because of your victory over other wights, Eriac believes Reykur may be waiting for you.\n2\tTalk to Eriac at the Eglan-camp in Agamaur\tEriac awaits you at the Eglan-camp in the southern reaches of Agamaur. You have killed Reykur, throwing the remnant of the wight-army into confusion. Eriac will want to hear of your success.\n",
[3835]="70043DEC\n1\tDefeat Morgul Captains and War-leaders (total: 5)\tMorgul Captains and War-leaders can be found in enemy strongholds in Osgiliath. You should defeat Morgul Captains and War-leaders.\n2\tSpeak with Melethon\tMelethon is at the Causeway Forts. You should speak to Melethon.\n",
[3836]="700397E3\n1\tSearch haystacks (total: 6)\tHaystacks can be found throughout the farm south-east of Middlemead. You have heard curious rustling coming from the haystacks at a farm outside Middlemead. You should investigate to discern if the Dunlendings have infiltrated the farm.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have investigated several haystacks and found a few Dunlendings hiding amidst the straw.\n",
[3837]="7001E993\n1\tGather pieces of wood (total: 5)\030Gather water samples (total: 3)\tSâd Doldúr lies to the south of Barad Angol, down the mountainside. Himeinior has asked you to collect some water samples and pieces of fallen blighted wood from the area around Sâd Doldúr.\n2\tTalk to Himeinior\tHeiminior is at the camp near Barad Angol, up the mountain pass north of Sâd Doldúr. You should return the branches and samples of water to Himeinior.\n",
[3838]="70000DEF\n1\tFind Daffodil\tTroll's Knoll is in Rushock Bog, south-east of Needlehole. Filibert suspects that Olwir took Daffodil out into Rushock Bog somewhere. He suggested you start searching at Troll's Knoll.\n2\tExamine the cow\tAs you searched Troll's Knoll on behalf of Filibert Bolger, you came across the corpse of a cow. A closer examination of the cow should reveal if it is Filibert's cow, Daffodil.\n3\tBring the cow bell to Filibert Bolger\030Collect the cow bell\tFilibert Bolger can be found in Needlehole, north of Troll's Knoll. In your examination of the dead cow you found atop Troll's Knoll, you came across a bell. Perhaps Filibert Bolger will be able to tell from the bell whether the cow you found was his Daffodil.\n",
[3839]="70042FC1\n1\tSearch for Dagor\tDagor ran south-eastward out of Arnach. Baranor has asked you to venture out and find Dagor and the men who followed him.\n2\tGather stones for a cairn (total: 6)\tStones for a cairn can be found around the clearing where Dagor and his men died, due east of Arnach. You found Dagor's lifeless corpse. It is clear that he died a soldier's death. You should give him and his men a heroes' rite and build a cairn where they fell.\n3\tBuild a cairn\tStones for a cairn can be found around the clearing where Dagor died, south-east of Arnach. You found Dagor's lifeless corpse. It is clear that he died a soldier's death. You should give him and his men a heroes' rite and build a cairn where they fell.\n4\tMourn Dagor's corpse\tDagor and his newly-built cairn lie in a clearing south-east of Arnach. You found Dagor's lifeless corpse. It is clear that he died a soldier's death. You should give him and his men a heroes' rite and mourn their passing.\n5\tTalk to Baranor\tBaranor stands within the keep in Arnach. You found the lifeless corpses of Dagor and his men. It is clear that he died a soldier's death. You should return to Baranor and tell him of how you built a cairn and mourned his loss.\n",
[3840]="70042EDC\n1\tDefeat Haradrim Captains (total: 3)\tHaradrim Captains can be found, especially in their camps, east and south of Arnach. You should defeat captains of the Haradrim to compromise their leadership and organization.\n2\tTalk to Dagor\tDagor can be found in Arnach, near the keep. You should return to Dagor and tell him how you have bested a number of their leaders.\n",
})
